# Which audited artifacts THIS BRANCH is expected to resolve.
#
# The audit tests assert the verdict that matches the artifact on the classpath: a pinned artifact
# must certify with its exact shape proof, anything else must refuse. Deciding which arm to take
# from the artifact ITSELF means a dependency bump silently swaps every audit test from "prove the
# shape" to "prove it refuses", and the suite stays green over zero shape coverage. That is not
# hypothetical: it is what the mc-26.2 branch was doing -- twelve green gate tests, nothing proved.
#
# So the expectation lives here, outside the thing being measured. Change a dependency version and
# the tests go RED until someone edits this file deliberately and says why.
#
#   pinned   = this branch resolves the exact audited artifact; the shape proof must pass
#   unpinned = this branch resolves something else; the audit must refuse and name the drift
servercore=pinned
rabbit-pathfinding-fix=pinned
fabric-events-interaction-v0=pinned
fabric-content-registries-v0=pinned

# THIS BRANCH IS AUDITED FOR 26.3.
#
# Re-derived against the artifacts 26.3 resolves: servercore 1.5.20+26.3 (pinned by its Modrinth
# version id LCG1Bm84, because that version number also exists as a NeoForge build),
# rabbit-pathfinding-fix 1.5.0, and Fabric API 0.162.0+26.3 (events-interaction 5.3.7+b9b88df45d,
# content-registries 15.0.4+74ed1ea55d). Every shape proof passed on those bytes with no change.
# Both Fabric modules are pinned in two packaging forms: the standalone artifact a dev environment
# resolves and the recompressed copy nested in the aggregate fabric-api jar, which a real install
# loads. On 26.2 those were byte-identical; on 26.3 they are not.
#
# NOT listed here and NOT audited on 26.3: lithium. Its 0.26.2 build changes three of the eight
# audited classes, so the proofs behind those pins have not been re-run; see
# LithiumPathfindingCompatibility. It is absent rather than "unpinned" because this file is read only
# for artifacts on the unit-test classpath, and Lithium is not on it.
